// Volumes: one display set for each acquisition.
//
// A CT, MR, PT or NM series that holds more than one AcquisitionNumber gives
// one display set for each AcquisitionNumber, in AcquisitionNumber order, and
// not in time order. The display set gets the attribute `acquisitionNumber`.
//
// The file changes the `groupBy` and the `attributes` of `volume3d`, and not
// its `sortBy`, so it works together with `volumePositionOrder`, in either
// order: one volume for each acquisition, with the slices in position order.
// `volume3d` has no `attributes`, so the file uses `$set` there and not
// `$merge`.
//
// A series with one AcquisitionNumber gives one display set, as without the
// file.
//
// Some CT scanners give a new AcquisitionNumber to each rotation of an axial
// (step) scan. Such a series gives one display set for each rotation.
//
// A 4D series that gives each time point its own AcquisitionNumber (for
// example MR perfusion) gives one display set for each time point.
{
  "displaySetRules": {
    "volume3d": {
      "groupBy": { "$set": ["SeriesInstanceUID", "AcquisitionNumber"] },
      "attributes": { "$set": { "acquisitionNumber": "AcquisitionNumber" } }
    }
  }
}
